---
/**
 * The portal hero.
 *
 * Three real grid columns — photo air, headline, news rail — inside a box whose
 * bottom padding is reserved for the module deck that rides up over it. The
 * only absolutely positioned things in here are the photograph and the dot
 * field, neither of which carries text.
 */
---

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
  <img
    class="hero-photo"
    src="/assets/shore-hero.jpg"
    alt=""
    width="736"
    height="520"
    style="object-position: 30% 72%;"
    fetchpriority="high"
    decoding="async"
  />
  <div class="hero-dots" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="hero-stamp">DEVELOPER PREVIEW ✦ 0.0.2</p>

    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">NATIVE HOST / WASM COMPONENTS</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">
        <span class="line-a">run the guest.</span>
        own the machine.
      </h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        A WebAssembly component describes a semantic interface. The native host keeps authority over
        layout, input, accessibility, rendering, and failure.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-news" aria-label="What is active">
      <h2>pre-0.3</h2>
      <p><b>Phase 3:</b> the host-owned text boundary is taking shape.</p>
      <a href="/blog/phase-3-pre-0-3">Read the release note ▸</a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
